bound-lock/1 about="Admit another device into a place, once whoever holds its root says yes: the key its own key tool handed, under a name, covering what is given — without it, what a member is: asking, keeping what it read, proving access. What it claims to cover is not read." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/admit value=place|key|name|coverage
bound-lock/1 about="Allow one offer that is not of class read, up to a number of times." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=prompt/can value=source|operation|times
bound-lock/1 about="An API already says what it offers, where it is reached and how access to it is proven. head reads that document once, compiles it into lines its place pins by digest, and from then on answers by those lines: which operation reads, what it asks, what it answered. It names no kind of source and no client: what it reads is said by the worlds it adopts, and what it asks through is what the client declares. [Connect any API](docs/connect-any-api.md) shows each level of access on a real public API.\n\nA person does three things. **Found a place**: a folder whose lock is the place, its root key kept in the keychain. **Connect a source**: hand head an API document, and an overlay beside it when it says too little; it is compiled once, pinned, and every offer is listed with its class. **Ask**: read an operation. head obtains access the first time, as the document declares it, calls only what reads, types the answer and lands a receipt.\n\nAccess comes at three levels, and the place says which. **None**: the document states a read needs nothing, and nothing is asked. **A declared flow**: the document, or its overlay, declares how access is obtained, as an Arazzo profile: a form, a one-time code, a choice, a provider's page. head runs it once per issuer and keeps only the token, in the keychain. **A secret entered by hand**: a key or a password, only where the place's root allows it, entered on head's own one-time page and never through the model.\n\nWhat head never does. It never guesses how access is proven: a document that does not state it is said so, and nothing is called. It never calls an operation that is not a read without the person's yes, nor past what the place allows; a place that would stand on another's lock as its parent is refused by name, since composing two places' policies is bound's. It never lets a secret reach the model, a file, an answer or an argument. And it never raises a ceiling to make room: what outgrows one is split by responsibility." at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/idea value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An MCP server that reads any API by its document: access asked once per issuer, every answer typed by the world that compiled it, every read kept with a signed receipt." at=policy:head/docs by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/what value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An earlier call of {operation} on {source} landed its intent {intent} and no receipt: look at what it would have changed with closes={intent}, then act again." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=said/open value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="An intent an earlier act left open, by the scope it was named under: once this read lands, it closes that intent with the read-s digest. Look at what the act would have changed." at=policy:head/surface by=target form=alphabet measure=id role=writes scope=tool/look/closes value=string
